The {{Term/Store|Kochi Dye Shop||Series, BotW, TotK, AoC}},{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK, AoC}}<ref>{{Cite|- Kochi Dye Shop -<br/>We live to dye!|Sign|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|- Kochi Dye Shop -<br/>Supports your stylish life.|Sign|TotK}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Kochi Dye Shop}}|Map|AoC}}</ref> also known as the '''Dye Shop''',{{Exp Game|BotW, TotK}}<ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Monk Blue|'''Dye Shop'''}}|Map|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Color TotK|Map Blue|'''Dye Shop'''}}|Map|TotK}}</ref> is a recurring location in {{TLoZ Series}}.

==Features and Overview==
==={{BotW|-}}===
The Kochi Dye Shop is located in [[Hateno Village]]. It is the only [[Shop]] of its kind in [[Hyrule]]. [[Sayge]] operates the Dye Shop itself, while his wife, [[Senna]], greets visitors outside.<ref>{{Cite|I'm the hardest working greeter there is. Though it hardly seems like work when the weather's so nice...|Senna|BotW}}</ref> At night, their son [[Sefaro]] sleeps in one of the Shop's [[Bed]]s, muttering about a [[Sheikah]] girl.<ref>{{Cite|Snnnrrmm... Zzz... Nnggg... A {{Color BotW|Red|girl from the Sheikah tribe}}... Zzz...|Sefaro|BotW}}</ref>

At the Kochi Dye Shop, Sayge can use [[Hateno Dye]]s to change the color of [[Link]]'s [[Armor]].<ref>{{Cite|Welcome! If you were looking to add some color to your wardrobe, you found the right place! Hue do you do? Welcome to {{Color BotW|Blue|Kochi Dye Shop}}, where we live to dye!|Sayge|BotW}}</ref> The procedure costs 20 [[Rupee]]s, but Link must provide five [[Material]]s of matching color as well.<ref>{{Cite|If you have any {{Color BotW|Blue|dye ingredients}}, it's {{Color BotW|Red|20 rupees}} to dye an item... That includes our service charge, of course.|Sayge|BotW}}</ref> In the past, the Kochi Dye Shop would be able to prepare these Materials themselves, but the increased number of [[Monster]]s has made their collection difficult.<ref>{{Cite|{{Color BotW|Blue|Hateno dyeing}} is a tradition craft of Hateno Village. In days past, we'd use our own prepared {{Color BotW|Blue|dye ingredients}}. But these days, there are so many {{Color BotW|Blue|monsters}} about, that it's difficult for us to gather {{Color BotW|Blue|ingredients}}...|Sayge|BotW}}</ref> As a result, the Shop started allowing customers to bring their own Materials, with the addition of a service charge.<ref>{{Cite|That's why we switched to the customer bringing us the {{Color BotW|Blue|dye ingredients}}, and in return, we have a small service charge.|Sayge|BotW}}</ref> As is tradition in Hateno Village, Link's entire outfit will be Dyed at once.<ref>{{Cite|Get ready! Because we are going to dye all the clothes you're wearing at once!|Sayge|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|It's the Hateno tradition to dye a person's {{Color BotW|Red|whole outfit}}, from head to toe, all at once!|Sayge|BotW}}</ref> Sayge is also able to restore Link's Armor to its original appearance.<ref>{{Cite|[Back to the original.] Wonderful. Now go wait up there. I'll just be a minute.|Sayge|BotW}}</ref>

When Link decides to Dye his Armor, he will be transported to the nearby platform, where Sayge prompts him to either choose a Hateno Dye color or change his Armor.<ref>{{Cite|All right, choose your {{Color BotW|Blue|dye color}} or go ahead and {{Color BotW|Blue|change clothes}}!|Sayge|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|All right! Choose your {{Color BotW|Blue|dye color}} wisely! Or do you want to change clothes again?|Sayge|BotW}}</ref> If Link is wearing Armor that cannot be Dyed, Sayge will warn him of this fact.<ref>{{Cite|You're wearing some clothes you {{Color BotW|Blue|actually can't dye}}! Is that OK?|Sayge|BotW}}</ref> After selecting a Dye color, Sayge then asks for five Materials that match.<ref>{{Cite|Choose {{Color BotW|Red|five}} ingredients you'd like to use in your dye!|Sayge|BotW}}</ref> He then asks Link for his 20 Rupee payment.<ref>{{Cite|OK then, that'll be {{Color BotW|Red|20 rupees}}!|Sayge|BotW}}</ref> Once everything has been finalized, Sayge thanks Link and instructs him to stay still,<ref>{{Cite|Thanks for the business! All right now... Stay like that and don't move a muscle!|Sayge|BotW}}</ref> at which point he drops him and his Materials into the basin below. When Link leaves the basin, his entire outfit will have been Dyed.<ref>{{Cite|Yeeho! We made something very special here if I do say so myself!|Sayge|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Wow! Absolutely chromatic!|Sayge|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|Yeehoo! What a wonderful tone that is! I might try that out on one of my outfits!|Sayge|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|You look dashing!|Sayge|BotW}}</ref> Sayge will also offer to redo the Dye if Link dislikes it.<ref>{{Cite|And?! How is it? Do you find this palette-able? If you'd like to do a redye, just let me know!|Sayge|BotW}}</ref>

